3.2 Folder structure

src/
  api/            (use fetch, API call functions)
  components/     (reusable UI: Button, Avatar, MessageBubble, etc.)
  pages/          (Login, Register, Workspace, Channel)
  context/        (AuthContext, WorkspaceContext)
  hooks/          (useAuth, useChannel, useMessages)
  App.jsx
  main.jsx


  3.3 Set up API client with auth



Points to your Laravel API base URL
Attaches the Sanctum token to headers automatically
Handles 401s (redirect to login)
3.4 Build pages in this order
Login/Register pages — connect to Sanctum endpoints, store token
Workspace list/create page — after login, show/create workspaces
Channel sidebar — list channels in the selected workspace
Message view — list messages in selected channel (plain fetch, no real-time yet), input box to post new message
DM view — same pattern, for 1:1 messages

Milestone check: you can log in, pick a workspace, click a channel, see messages, post a new message, and it appears after a manual refresh. No real-time yet — that's intentional, get this rock solid first.